# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LINE ENDINGS ARE DECIDED BY THIS REPO, NOT BY WHOEVER CHECKED IT OUT.
#
# core.autocrlf=true was in effect here from the SYSTEM gitconfig
# (C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig) — the Git-for-Windows installer default.
# It was set in NEITHER this repository NOR the user's global config, so the
# rule deciding every file's bytes on disk was recorded nowhere a reader could
# find it, and the same commits produced different working trees on different
# machines. That is what this file fixes: the decision now lives in the repo.
#
# The index was ALREADY 100% LF when this file was added — 410 of 410 tracked
# text files, zero CRLF, zero mixed (git ls-files --eol, 2026-08-27, HEAD
# 5aa4c9c). So this file changed NO blob and NO history: git add --renormalize
# staged nothing but this file, and git blame is untouched.
#
# What was broken is the CHECKOUT side, and only that. A fresh clone
# materialised all 410 text files as CRLF. That is the class behind four
# incidents on the Wave 0 arc, one of which DEFEATED A GUARD-PROOF: a
# $-anchored regex silently no-ops against CRLF because JavaScript's '.' does
# not match '\r', so the match fails and the code carries on with unstripped
# text. Five guards once reported PASS on the resulting broken parse.
#
# ⚠ VERIFY THIS FILE'S EFFECT WITH `git ls-files --eol`.
#   NOT `git status` — it reads through the clean filter and reports an empty
#   diff while every file on disk is still CRLF.
#   NOT Git Bash `grep` — it strips CR in text mode and reported 0 matches on
#   a file carrying 91 of them.
#   Both were observed lying during the change that added this file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

* text=auto eol=lf

# The 11 tracked binaries are all correctly auto-detected today: a full
# renormalization was rehearsed in a throwaway clone and all 11 hashes came
# through intact. These three lines are belt-and-braces — detection is a
# content heuristic re-evaluated per blob, and a binary corrupted by an eol
# filter is not repairable in place.
# ⚠ .ico is listed because there IS one tracked (public/favicon.ico).
#   PRE_LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md:1593 proposes only .png/.woff2 — two extensions
#   where three are needed.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff2 binary
